  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Training on Assistive Products Pilot Project.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Delivery of in-country project activities related to training and mentoring</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Facilitate the monitoring and evaluation of the project, including leading the data collection, to inform further development of tools and planning of future in-country activities related to strengthening access to AT.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Participate in the planning of in-country project activities in collaboration with other partners (WHO, MOHCDGEC, PO-RALG)</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to improve access to quality health and care for older people, including training primary health care workforce to provide age friendly the health and care services to older people by introducing the provision of simple assistive products, such as walking aids, reading glasses and shower chairs, at primary health care level for older people as well as people living with disabilities and chronic conditions in Morogoro, Tanzania.</narrative>
  </description>
